+
+## Generic homebrew development updates
+
+This local fork supports an opt-in companion directory for any `.wuhb` under
+`sd:/wiiu/apps/`, including subdirectories. There is no per-game registration.
+Keep the original WUHB at the same path: its path and metadata continue to select
+its save directory, and its content remains the fallback for unchanged files.
+
+Example:
+
+```text
+sd:/wiiu/apps/Kirby Triple Deluxe.wuhb
+sd:/wiiu/apps/Kirby Triple Deluxe.wuhb.dev/
+  active.txt                         # contains: build-20261118-1
+  builds/build-20261118-1/
+    root.rpx                         # rebuilt executable, any original RPX name
+    content/
+      shaders.idx                    # optional changed content files only
+      shaders.gsh
+```
+
+At launch, the module reads the companion's `active.txt`, validates the release
+component and RPX header, prepares that RPX, and mounts the original WUHB.
+A content **merge** layer overrides only files present in the selected release.
+Missing files still come from the WUHB; saves use the original bundle's path and
+metadata. An executable-only update needs no `content` directory. This does not
+load an entire OS, patch an installed retail title, or convert executable formats.
+A merge cannot express deletion of a file already present in the bundle.
+
+Use `tools/ftp_homebrew_dev.py` in our 3Dii U checkout to publish an update:
+
+```sh
+python3 tools/ftp_homebrew_dev.py WII_U_IP \
+  'wiiu/apps/Kirby Triple Deluxe.wuhb' rebuilt/g_bale.rpx \
+  --content changed-content --release build-20261118-1
+```
+
+The publisher uploads to a new immutable release directory, checks every file by
+SHA-256 readback, and publishes `active.txt` last. It checks that both shader files
+are supplied together. If activation fails, it restores the old marker. Upload or
+verification failures leave the prior active release selected. Existing releases
+are never overwritten; use a new release ID to retry an interrupted transfer.
+The original WUHB and save folders are never uploaded, renamed, or deleted.
+A brief gap during FTP's two-step marker rename uses the original bundle.
+
+The updated module must be loaded by reloading Aroma once. Future data updates
+take effect on the next launch, without rebuilding the module. Reloading Aroma is
+not required after each RPX/content update. Treat content as read-only; a homebrew
+application's mutable state belongs in its save directory.
+
+Keep shader files and their RPX from the same build. Versioned upload mechanics
+prevent partially uploaded releases from activating; they cannot establish whether
+an arbitrary rebuilt binary is compatible with its original game assets.
+
+For compatibility, the older Brain Age and Mario Party override paths still work
+when no companion `active.txt` is present. They are not an allowlist for the new
+system. Remove or rename `active.txt` to launch the bundled executable (except for
+those legacy titles, which will then use their older override if present).
